    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1080">

                <pb facs="1605" n="1585" sameAs="frus:frus1950v07/pg1585"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">795.00/12–2150: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Korea</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Muccio</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Seoul</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-12-21T14:00:00+09:00">December 21,
                            1950—2 p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 21—2:26 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>596. Embtel 585, December 18. During past 3
                    days UN forces in Eighth Army sector continued out of contact with CCF. Light contact was maintained, however, with
                    North Korean forces in 38th parallel area ranging from due north of Seoul to
                    slightly east of Chunchon. Most significant development during 3 day period has
                    been receipt of <pb facs="1606" n="1586" xml:id="pg1586"/> intelligence reports
                    indicating movement of CCF forces southeast from
                    Pyongyang area and south from Koksan area toward parallel areas opposite
                    Uijongou and Chunchon corridors leading to Seoul. These reports, while not firm,
                    suggest there may be from 1 to 2 CCF armies
                    deploying north of parallel. Unfortunately, visibility has been so poor past 3
                    nights that vehicles sightings have been inconclusive.</p>
                <p>Communist air activity has been slight past 3 days. There were no sightings on
                    eighteenth and twentieth; there were 2 sightings on nineteenth, one of which
                    included two Migs observed as far south as Pyongyang.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Muccio</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
